# React UI

- Follow the existing functional-component and React Hooks patterns. Keep state near its owner; reuse the current Context and reducer patterns for state shared across components.
- Preserve the current React Router 6 route definitions and existing route behavior.
- Keep desktop, mobile, pointer, and touch behavior in mind when changing UI or input handling.
- Reuse existing SCSS files, variables, and component styles. Avoid unrelated global-style changes.
- Keep event listeners and other external effects paired with cleanup in the effect that creates them.
- Add or update focused tests for observable behavior when appropriate; the project uses React Testing Library and Jest.
